    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n27 Bellevue Park is a superb four-bedroom semi-detached family home extending to approximately 150 sq.m (1,615 sq.ft), occupying a prime position within this highly regarded Greystones neighbourhood set moments from Church Road. Beautifully proportioned throughout, the accommodation offers an ideal balance of living and bedroom space, creating the perfect setting for both everyday family life and entertaining.\n\nOne enters through the front door to a notably wide entrance hallway which open to an elegantly proportioned, dual aspect sitting / dining room with feature brick fireplace. A further versatile reception room facing the front of the residence is complete with built in storage and would make an ideal home office or dedicated playroom. To the rear of the home a wonderfully bright kitchen/dining area flows seamlessly into a light filled sunroom overlooking the private west facing rear garden, which enjoys excellent sunshine throughout the afternoon and evening and provides an enjoyable outdoor retreat. The downstairs guest WC completes the ground floor accommodation, and a light filled landing with Stira access to the attic opens to 4 well appointed double bedrooms and family bathroom.\n\nBellevue Park is renowned for its exceptional convenience, with Greystones Town Centre, the marina, seafront, schools, sporting amenities and an excellent range of shops, cafés and restaurants all within easy reach, while the Dart station and N11 ensure effortless connectivity for commuters. Families seeking an active seaside lifestyle will appreciate proximity to an excellent selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools. The nearby Shoreline Leisure Centre, sports clubs including golf, tennis, rugby and sailing plus playgrounds and coastal amenities provide endless opportunities for recreation, while the surrounding network of walking and cycling routes encourages an outdoor lifestyle.\n\nCombining generous accommodation, a highly desirable orientation and an outstanding location, this is a home of immense appeal in one of Greystones' most sought-after residential settings. The neighbourhood is known for its strong sense of community, well-maintained surroundings and attractive streetscape, making it a desirable place to put down roots.\n\n Viewing can be arranged through MySherryFitz or by contacting the Greystones office on (01) 287 4005."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nA wide entrance with frosted glass blending privacy and solar gain.\n\nLiving / Dining Room - 3.49m x 8.02m\nA dual aspect reception with feature brick fireplace and timber mantle and electric inset. Door to sunroom.\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room - 4.46m x 3.02m\nFloor and eye level units, stainless steel sink and drainer, tiled splashback. Integrated electric hob, oven, grill, extractor fan, microwave. Opening to:\n\nSun Room - 3.48m x 2.60m\nWall light, laminate wooden flooring, door to rear garden.\n\nPlayroom/Home Office - 2.37m x 4.77m\nFacing the front garden, a versatile space with built in storage units.\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - \nStira access to attic, frosted window on gable.\n\nMain Bedroom 1 - 3.74m x 5.33m\nGenerous double with large window overlooking front garden, built in wardrobe and pedestal wash hand basin with wall mounted mirror above.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.20m x 3.18m\nA large double to the front of the property\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.78m x 3.01m\nDouble to rear with hilltop outlook. Currently laid out as home office / study with extensive built in shelved storage.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.07m x 1.78m\nFully tiled walls and floor, WC, heated chrome towel rail, pedestal wash hand basin, frosted window. Bath with dual shower attachments.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.75m x 3.45m\nA double bedroom with wooden plank floorboards and hilltop views looking west to the rear.\n\nHot Press - \nShelved for storage\n\nOutside - \nTarmac and cobble block off street car parking to the front with mature hedged boundaries to the front and side providing attractive green screening. Gated side access to a beautifully private west facing rear garden, laid out in lawn with Indian sandstone patio providing the perfect spot for sunbathing and entertaining. Mature greenery in gravel beds with well defined borders. Block built shed storage and garden tap.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Special Features:</li><li>Well-appointed four bedroom semi-detached home</li><li>Highly convenient location</li><li>Short walk to all village amenities including Dart</li><li>West facing rear garden</li><li>Off street car parking</li><li>No management fees</li><li>Chain free sale</ul>"
      },
